# Active Directory Environment

## Overview

The CyberLab includes a Microsoft Active Directory environment designed to provide realistic identity, authentication, and endpoint telemetry for security monitoring and attack simulation.

The Active Directory domain is:

```text
cyberlab.test
```

NetBIOS domain:

```text
CYBERLAB
```

---

## Active Directory Architecture

The CyberLab Active Directory environment provides identity, authentication,
DNS, and security telemetry for the Windows systems in the range.

```text
                       cyberlab.test
                            |
                  +---------+---------+
                  |                   |
                  |       DC01        |
                  |    10.20.0.50     |
                  |                   |
                  |  Active Directory |
                  |       DNS         |
                  +---------+---------+
                            |
                            |
                  CyberLab 10.20.0.0/24
                            |
          +-----------------+-----------------+
          |                                   |
          |                                   |
+---------+----------+              +---------+----------+
|     W11-Attack     |              |      OPNsense      |
|                    |              |                    |
| Domain Workstation |              | Gateway / Firewall |
|       DHCP         |              |    10.20.0.1       |
+--------------------+              +--------------------+
```

### Core Systems

| System | Role | Address |
|---|---|---|
| **DC01** | Domain Controller / DNS | `10.20.0.50` |
| **W11-Attack** | Domain-joined workstation | DHCP |
| **OPNsense** | Gateway / Firewall | `10.20.0.1` |
| **Wazuh** | SIEM / XDR | `10.20.0.60` |

